  "E10" [label="(34,0,0) Currently special mechanical self-organisation at the jamming point leads to density and contact-number hyperuniformity, reflecting an essential difference in marginal stability between marginally jammed and conventional over-jammed states."];
  "E11" [label="(1,0,0) Currently hyperuniform systems are characterised by a vanishing density spectrum χv(q) at low wavenumbers, setting them apart from ordinary liquids and disordered solids."];
